### 3. Mathematical Formulation of the NTS-SASP/SoH Model

The engine models the evolution of a lesion's state space across time \\(t\\) and spatial coordinates \\(\mathbf{x}\\):

#### Equation 1: Paracrine Secretome Field Diffusion (\\(C_{SASP}\\))
\\[\frac{\partial C_{SASP}(\mathbf{x}, t)}{\partial t} = D_{SASP} \nabla^2 C_{SASP}(\mathbf{x}, t) + \alpha \cdot \rho_{senescent}(\mathbf{x}, t) - \gamma_{senomorphic}(t) \cdot C_{SASP}(\mathbf{x}, t)\\]
* \\(D_{SASP}\\): Diffusion coefficient of pro-inflammatory cytokines (IL-6, IL-1\\(\beta\\), MMPs) through the extracellular matrix.
* \\(\rho_{senescent}\\): Local density of treatment-induced senescent glia/tumor cells.
* \\(\gamma_{senomorphic}\\): Damping rate induced by supportive therapies (e.g., dexamethasone or senomorphic agents like rapamycin/JAK inhibitors).

#### Equation 2: Cumulative Tissue State-of-Health (\\(\text{SoH}_{tissue}\\))
\\[\text{SoH}_{tissue}(\mathbf{x}, t) = \text{SoH}_0 - \int_0^t \left( \beta \cdot \dot{D}_{RT}(\mathbf{x}, \tau) + \eta \cdot C_{SASP}(\mathbf{x}, \tau) + \lambda \cdot \text{Load}_{chemo}(\tau) \right) d\tau\\]
* \\(\dot{D}_{RT}\\): Spatial dose rate delivered from the DICOM-RT planning grid (\\(>60\text{ Gy}\\) high-dose regions).
* When \\(\text{SoH}_{tissue}(\mathbf{x}, t)\\) drops below a critical threshold \\(\text{SoH}_{crit}\\) while \\(C_{SASP}\\) is high, the engine flags **Radiation Necrosis / Pseudoprogression** rather than true tumor recurrence.

